    "candidate_scope": "Only Ci128/Co128/Kw11 uses the bounded reciprocal in the B preload quotient: twelve hotspot layers and three dilation tuples. Other widths/shapes retain original unsigned division. This changes address arithmetic, not shared-memory layout or the separate CPU staged32 transpose.",
    "proof": [
      "For the selected K=128*11=1408, k0 steps by32 through K-32 and r=i>>4 lies in0..31. Thus loaded k=k0+r lies in0..1407. The broader0..3583 domain was also checked independently; the16-bit mask preserves every admitted k.",
      "5958*11=65536+2. Write k=11q+r, with0<=r<=10 and q<=325 for k<=3583. Then k*5958/65536=q+(2q+5958r)/65536, and the remainder term is at most60230/65536<1. The shifted product equals floor(k/11) exactly; no correction is needed within this bound. Maximum product21,347,514 fits32bits; both multiplicands fit16bits.",
      "The specialization predicate confines the formula to K1408. All other width/shape specializations retain original unsigned division. The ncnn host and shader loop bounds remain unchanged; this does not promise arbitrary out-of-contract helper arguments.",
      "Identical ci gives identical k-ci*11, tap/dilation, pitch and x addresses. Floating operands/order, shared tiles, vector loads/stores, accumulators, workgroups, barriers, bindings, queue policy and hardware guards remain unchanged."
    ],
